Wait: there's an issue with `s.autoThrottle = input.autoThrottle;` — I wrote:
```
const auto = s.autoThrottle;
let throttle = input.throttle;
if (auto) throttle = 0.58;
if (input.autoThrottle !== auto) {
  s.autoThrottle = input.autoThrottle;
}
```
This is weird: s.autoThrottle reads its own stored value, but the source of truth should be input.autoThrottle (toggled by T key or CRUISE button). So just: `s.autoThrottle = input.autoThrottle; throttle = input.autoThrottle ? 0.58 : input.throttle;` Then manual keys adjust. But then "input.throttle = throttle" writes back so HUD can show. OK, simplify:

```
const auto = input.autoThrottle;
s.autoThrottle = auto;
let throttle = auto ? 0.58 : input.throttle;
if (input.throttleRaised) throttle += 0.55*dt;
if (input.throttleLowered) throttle -= 0.55*dt;
throttle = clamp(throttle, 0, 1);
input.throttle = throttle;
```

If manual keys used, throttle changes. Fine.

Also `land + 1.6` crash threshold — plane sits ~1 unit above ground? Plane origin is at fuselage center ~0.45. Add slight forgiveness: pos.y < land + 1.2 crash. Hmm plane pitch could clip terrain at high speed into hill. Fine: 1.5.

Fix that block. Also remove unused variables (pitchVel/rollVel are used; `this.pitchVel *= 1;` pointless, remove).

